    "body": "## Purpose\n\n`Cohere2MoeForCausalLM` never constructed a clamped activation. A checkpoint that sets `config.swiglu_limit` still built a bare `SiluAndMul()` and passed no limit into `FusedMoEFactory`, so the clamp never left the model definition.\n\nThis is model-definition plumbing only. No kernel change. It mirrors `Glm5NextMLP` / `Glm5NextMoE`:\n\n- dense and shared `Cohere2MoeMLP` take `swiglu_limit` and use `SiluAndMulWithClamp` when the field is set\n- the MoE block forwards the same value to `FusedMoEFactory`\n\nThis is **clamped SiLU** (`alpha=1.0`, `beta=0.0` defaults), not SwiGLU-OAI.\n\nWhen `swiglu_limit` is absent, behavior is unchanged: `SiluAndMul()`, and `FusedMoEFactory` receives `None`. No public Cohere checkpoint sets this field today; the PR enables a config field the architecture already documents, the same way GLM-5.Next does.\n\n## Merge ordering\n\nLanding this **before** [ROCm/aiter#6335](https://github.com/ROCm/aiter/pull/6335) is harmful on gfx942. Today the missing construction is inert. After this PR, `VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER_MOE=1` can send a real limit into `aiter.fused_moe`, land on CK two-stage, and have it **silently dropped**. #6335 is the fail-loud guard for that case. Please do not merge this ahead of that guard without a conscious decision.\n\nThis PR does **not** unblock the bf16 → CK path Cohere hits today. That still needs CK kernel work.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] Construction tests in `tests/models/test_cohere2_moe.py` (no GPU):\n  - config without `swiglu_limit` → `SiluAndMul`, factory receives `None`\n  - config with a finite limit → `SiluAndMulWithClamp` (alpha=1, beta=0) on dense/shared MLP, and the limit reaches `FusedMoEFactory`\n- [x] Wired into the CPU Basic Models Other job in `.buildkite/test_areas/models_basic.yaml`\n\n\nMade with [Cursor](https://cursor.com)",
